      "message": "Did you decide to go with SkDoubleVector because of the need for cross, dot, and length functions?\n\nSkVx.h has a dot() that is templated, and we can template cross() or add a double variant. `length()` and `normalize()` would be useful functions that can easily be defined in terms of the existing functions: `normalize(v) \u003d v / length(v)` and `length(v) \u003d sqrt(dot(v,v))`.\n\nAlthough it looks like we don\u0027t have isFinite() in SkVx, and you\u0027d have to add static helper functions in SkPath.cpp to handle the loading/unloading from 2 doubles to 2 floats whereas this lets you have `set()` and `asSkVector()`. So that could be enough that it\u0027s worth an extra header and type definition vs. making skvx::double2 more useful. WDYT?",
